+**Before you start**
+
+Paths in this preamble are relative to this skill's folder.
+
+1. Read the Principles section of the pstack principles index, `../poteto-mode/SKILL.md`. Before applying a principle, read its leaf skill at `../principle-<name>/SKILL.md`.
+2. Open a task list whose first items are this playbook's steps, copied verbatim. A step you skip stays on the list with `skip: <reason>`.
+3. Do not report done without runtime evidence: output from running the changed thing on the surface the task names. Tests or "it compiles" alone are not done.
+
+Reading the playbook: its relative links resolve from `./ (this skill's folder)`. "The installed plugin", `<plugin>` and "this pstack" mean the folder two levels up from this skill (`../..`), which holds `skills/` and `agents/`. The sections it cites (Non-negotiables, Subagents, Models, Writing the reply) are in the principles index; Opening a PR is `../poteto-mode/playbooks/opening-a-pr.md`. A skill it names that is not in your skill list is a file at `../<name>/SKILL.md`: read it instead of invoking it. When you spawn `pstack:poteto-agent`, give it the absolute path of `../poteto-mode/SKILL.md`. On Codex, map Claude tool and model names with `../poteto-mode/references/codex-tools.md`.
